# Frontend Services

## Rules

- One service file per backend module: `spec.service.ts`, `auth.service.ts`, `graph.service.ts`.
- All services use a shared `httpClient` instance (wrapper around `fetch`).
- No direct `fetch()` calls outside the services layer.
- Return typed responses matching `@kg/shared` DTOs.
- Throw typed errors from `@kg/shared` on failure — never swallow HTTP errors.
- Services are plain modules (not classes) — export named functions.

## Example

```typescript
import type { Spec, CreateSpecDto, SpecResponseDto } from '@kg/shared';
import { httpClient } from './http-client.js';

export async function createSpec(dto: CreateSpecDto): Promise<SpecResponseDto> {
  return httpClient.post<SpecResponseDto>('/api/specs', dto);
}

export async function getSpecById(id: string): Promise<Spec> {
  return httpClient.get<Spec>(`/api/specs/${id}`);
}
```

## Anti-patterns

- Calling `fetch()` directly in a component or store.
- Returning untyped `any` responses.
- Mixing service logic with UI concerns.
